From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: SOS bring-up <sos@localhost>
Date: Sun, 16 Aug 2026 09:56:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] s5e8825-common: Select no-Zygote base for SOS Core 1

The shared Samsung device definition unconditionally inherits
core_64_bit_only.mk, which assigns ro.zygote=zygote64. SOS Core 1 also used
core_no_zygote.mk, producing contradictory immutable vendor properties and a
hard build failure.

Select AOSP's existing no-Zygote product fragment at the shared hardware
boundary for the Core 1 shipping and provider-probe targets. All other a33x
products retain the original 64-bit Zygote configuration.
---
 common.mk | 8 +++++++-
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/common.mk b/common.mk
index 1233c99..010fad1 100644
--- a/common.mk
+++ b/common.mk
@@ -15,4 +15,10 @@
 
-# Inherit from generic products, most specific first
+# Inherit from generic products, most specific first. SOS Core 1 deliberately
+# retains the shared Samsung hardware product while selecting AOSP's empty
+# Zygote init configuration; every other a33x product remains 64-bit-only.
+ifneq ($(filter lineage_sos_core1_a33x lineage_sos_core1_dev_a33x,$(TARGET_PRODUCT)),)
+$(call inherit-product, $(SRC_TARGET_DIR)/product/core_no_zygote.mk)
+else
 $(call inherit-product, $(SRC_TARGET_DIR)/product/core_64_bit_only.mk)
+endif
 $(call inherit-product, $(SRC_TARGET_DIR)/product/full_base_telephony.mk)
-- 
